<title>GERMANY: German ABB '96 pretax profit rises.</title>
<headline>German ABB '96 pretax profit rises.</headline>
<dateline>MANNHEIM, Germany 1997-03-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Calendar 1996:</p>
<p>(in millions of marks unless stated)</p>
<p>    Group net profit			   121     vs 172</p>
<p>    Group pre-tax profit		     243     vs 196</p>
<p>    Group income from ord. activities    nil     vs 110</p>
<p>    Group sales				  8,675   vs 8,224</p>
<p>    Group cash flow			    498     vs 658</p>
<p>    Group depreciation			 311     vs 339</p>
<p>    Group investment			   283     vs 310</p>
<p>    Group equity				 959     vs 1,050</p>
<p>    Parent net profit			  126.2   vs 125.6</p>
<p>    Dividend				     19.25   vs 19.25 marks</p>
<p>    DVFA earnings per share		  27.09   vs 29.16 marks</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of the German subsidiary of the Swiss-Swedish engineering group is Asea Brown Boveri AG.</p>
<p>Chairman Michael Pohr said in a statement that the company's return on sales rose to 2.8 percent in 1996 from one percent the year before and would rise to six percent by the year 2000.</p>
<p>-- Bonn Newsroom, 49 228 26097 150</p>
</text>
